<title>RUSSIA: Russia sold 7.94 mln t gas outside CIS in March.</title>
<headline>Russia sold 7.94 mln t gas outside CIS in March.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 7.94 million tonnes of natural gas to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States in March, compared to 6.46 million within the Soviet Union's old borders, Interfax news agency said.</p>
<p>The agency, quoting figures from the Russian customs committee, gave no comparisons for the previous month or the previous year. It said exports outside the CIS were worth $866 million and exports inside the CIS were worth $573 million.</p>
<p>First quarter exports -- inside and outside the CIS -- totalled 41.65 million tonnes and were worth $4.49 billion.</p>
<p>Most Russian gas was exported to Ukraine, to Germany and to Italy, Interfax said.</p>
</text>
